Attribution
-----------
This project implements the memory architecture described in:

  "Hindsight is 20/20: Building Agent Memory that Retains, Recalls, and
  Reflects" - Latimer, Boschi, Neeser, Bartholomew, Srivastava, Wang,
  Ramakrishnan (arXiv:2512.12818).

Its prompt wording and pipeline structure are informed by the open-source
reference implementation at https://github.com/vectorize-io/hindsight
(MIT License, Copyright (c) 2025 Vectorize AI, Inc.), which this project is a
from-scratch Rust reimplementation of, not a derivative code port.

Vendored upstream sources
-------------------------
Prompt source files from the upstream reference are vendored verbatim under
`crates/rustsight-core/prompts/upstream/<tag>/` (pinned tag `v1.1.0`, commit
`a5a619b5ca59c5c39e0f96be6f7a31fabd136bd5`, released 2026-10-21) so the Rust
prompt builders in `crates/rustsight-core/src/prompts/upstream/` can be held to
byte-for-byte parity. Vendored files (retain/fact_extraction.py,
retain/entity_labels.py, consolidation/prompts.py, reflect/prompts.py +
tools.py + tools_schema.py + tokenization.py, search/temporal_extraction.py +
think_utils.py, engine/prompt_utils.py, and upstream's prompt tests) retain
their upstream content, including copyright notice, and are MIT
Licensed, Copyright (c) 2025 Vectorize AI, Inc. See
`crates/rustsight-core/prompts/upstream/PROMPTS_VERSION` for the pin and
`scripts/prompt-sync` for re-vendoring. The Rust builders are a translation of
those files' prompt-building logic; see
`crates/rustsight-core/prompts/upstream/DIVERGENCES.md` for intentional
differences.
